{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevStripGrowthFKV","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevStripGrowthFKV","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Basis.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Basis.Basic","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevStripGrowthBoxReduction"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevStripGrowthFKV.comparable_shape_of_periodic_ballBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevStripGrowthFKV.comparable_shape_of_periodic_ballBound","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevStripGrowthFKV.lean#L48-L70","doc":"**Comparability shape from the compact ratio bound.** Let the ratio `Φ/Ψ` be\nperiodic under an `ℝ`-basis `bas` of `ℂ` and satisfy the two-sided bound\n`‖Φ/Ψ‖ ≤ C`, `1/C ≤ ‖Φ/Ψ‖` on the closed fundamental ball (the FKV eq-22 input).\nThen, wherever `Ψ z ≠ 0`, the `FaddeevPhiStripGrowth.comparable` shape holds:\n`‖Φ z‖ ≤ C‖Ψ z‖` and `‖Ψ z‖ ≤ C‖Φ z‖`. The two-sided global ratio bound comes from\n`FaddeevStripGrowthBoxReduction.comparable_of_periodic_ballBound`; this file adds the\n`norm_div` conversion to the `Φ`/`Ψ` modulus inequalities. ","signatureChunk":0}]}